WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.310
- [Narrator] This social media platform

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.340
is a Russian state-owned
alternative to YouTube.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.630
The Kremlin has been promoting

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.190
the homegrown network, RuTube,

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:11.880
as part of a battle for
Russian users and their minds.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.990
That's because in the country

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.390
social media platforms
have increasingly become

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.520
one of the main sources of information

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.620
challenging state television.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.760
- YouTube is the most important platform

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.380
for millions of people.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.510
- [Narrator] So, we examine
the Russian video platform

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.090
at the center of the Kremlin's
push to attract users

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.860
away from foreign networks,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.840
limiting their access to independent news

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.403
during the war in Ukraine.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.520
Owned by a Russian state company,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.460
RuTube is a video platform
almost as old as YouTube

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.380
and visually very similar to it

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.456
and the Kremlin has been
outspoken about its potential.

00:00:46.456 --> 00:00:50.289
(speaker speaking in Russian)

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.160
Since the war in Ukraine started,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.140
YouTube has been one of the last sources

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.420
of alternative news in Russia.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.010
That's because Instagram and Facebook

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.900
are blocked in the country.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.880
That happened after
the parent company Meta

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.400
barred access to some
state channels in Europe,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.500
following requests from the European Union

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.000
and British authorities.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.100
YouTube remains available in Russia

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.220
but there are concerns
about its future there,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.170
especially after the Kremlin and RuTube

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.360
have been on a mission to draw people away

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.938
from the American network.

00:01:19.938 --> 00:01:23.460
(speaker speaking in Russian)

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.160
The company has partnered
with some popular vloggers

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.980
and offered content
creators 100% of the revenue

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.730
from ad views during the
first 40 days after joining.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.490
The incentive came after
YouTube paused monetization

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.850
in Russia as a response to
its aggression in Ukraine.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.830
This means vloggers can
no longer make money

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.440
from ad views from users in Russia.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.230
A month later, some popular
Russian celebrities and vloggers

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.800
who were on YouTube also
started using RuTube.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.750
The platform's usership has also grown

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.180
as the Kremlin encouraged
government departments,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.430
universities and
state-backed media outlets

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.244
to migrate their content
from YouTube to RuTube.

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:00.930
- [Male Voice] Top Blog.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.010
- [Narrator] And Moscow is investing

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.930
in a new generation of vloggers

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.450
with the program teaching
Russians how to become successful

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.700
on domestic platforms like RuTube.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.410
But the government support is one reason

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.750
some users don't feel like switching.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.920
- There is no trust to
anything made by the government

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.860
especially in order to replace something

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.397
already good and foreign.

00:02:21.397 --> 00:02:23.383
(speaking in Russian)

00:02:23.383 --> 00:02:25.290
- [Narrator] Leionid Pashkowski
is a Russian speaking

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.700
travel blogger and journalist

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.130
with more than 1 million
followers on YouTube.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:31.200
He says he's skeptical about RuTube

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.870
replacing YouTube for Russian viewers.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.060
- I just tried to watch something

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.770
or find something in there

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:41.820
and there was no views
counters under the videos.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.010
- [Narrator] And data from
analytics firm, Similarweb

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.640
shows that there are fewer
users on RuTube than on YouTube.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.550
In May, RuTube had some 38 million visits,

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.730
a number dwarfed by the nearly
2 billion visits to YouTube

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.843
only from Russia.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.600
Some users can be put off by RuTube

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.400
because of censorship concerns

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.250
which begin to emerge
when uploading a video.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.070
According to RuTube's
content curation info page,

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:08.760
getting a video on the platform
can take up to 24 hours

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.860
as its moderation team watches every video

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.080
before other users can access it.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.720
And RuTube says, "It adheres
to the observance of the law

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.177
and generally accepted norms of morality."

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.730
It couldn't be determined if all videos

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.550
go through human creation
or how the platform decides

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.700
what videos to check
manually or automatically.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.811
- Any type of independent
creators and political activists

00:03:30.811 --> 00:03:33.240
cannot rely on RuTube.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.490
- [Narrator] Gregory Asmolov
studies the Russian internet

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.230
at King's College London.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.360
He says, even if content
that's not aligned

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.880
with the Kremlin's rhetoric
made it onto YouTube,

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.100
its algorithms wouldn't promote it.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.430
- And that's why YouTube is used by those

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.500
who are willing to find some kind of space

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.910
to express their voice.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.950
- [Narrator] YouTube also curates content.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.140
According to the company's
community guidelines,

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.840
its policies prohibit hate
speech, misinformation

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.970
and harmful or dangerous content.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.520
YouTube also says it uses human moderators

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.890
and an upload process
that automatically screens

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.200
for potential issues before posting.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.090
But the uploading time is faster

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.640
and the company says it can
take anywhere from a few minutes

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.553
to several hours based on
the file size and bandwidth.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.540
YouTube didn't comment on its
content moderation criteria

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.910
and the challenge from RuTube in Russia.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.360
- YouTube definitely is
still serving in Russia.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.860
- [Narrator] The American
tech giant has said

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.050
it's important to let
people in Russia have access

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.490
to independent news.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.080
- YouTube will be blocked.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.950
People in Russia will
be closed in a bubble

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:39.950
of just Russian information
and just propaganda.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.420
- [Narrator] RuTube and its
parent company Gazprom-Media

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.060
didn't respond to a request
for comment about censorship

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.890
and view count concerns.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.020
The Kremlin said its promotion of RuTube

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.480
started long before
the conflict in Ukraine

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.390
as it's always seen the
potential of the platform.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.420
As RuTube tries to gain
momentum and take on YouTube,

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.580
internet media experts say it'll require

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.170
a really important quality

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:04.050
that's one of the most
difficult to replicate.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.260
- That lacks the global spirit
of user generated content

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.700
that you can see on YouTube.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.800
Therefore, we can see
that YouTube continues

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.540
to be extremely popular in Russia

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.690
and RuTube is not able to replace YouTube

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.493
as a local alternative.

